<title>CHINA: China's May cereal exports detailed.</title>
<headline>China's May cereal exports detailed.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table shows cereal export figures from five major Chinese customs offices as well as the country of destinations in January-May.</p>
<p>Details were provided by the General Administration of Customs of China.</p>
<p>Figures are in tonnes. Percentages represent the share of the total market. Percentages may not add up to 100 percent because details of some smaller export destinations and supplying countries have not been included.</p>
<p>------WHEAT</p>
<p>    May exports:    0.2    Jan-May total export	19.2</p>
<p> CUSTOMS		 May	 Pct	   Jan-May	Pct</p>
<p>    Beijing		0	 0.0		 19	 98.9</p>
<p>    Huangpu		0.2   100.0		  0.2	1.0</p>
<p>DESTINATIONS</p>
<p>    Malaysia	     0.2    88.5		  0.2	1.0</p>
<p>    Japan		  0	 0.0		 19	 98.9</p>
<p>------BARLEY</p>
<p>    May exports     60     Jan-May total exports  5,562</p>
<p> CUSTOMS	     May	  Pct	   Jan-May	 Pct</p>
<p>    Dalian	    60	100.0	   5,562	  100.0</p>
<p>DESTINATIONS</p>
<p>    North Korea     60	100.0	   5,562	  100.0</p>
<p>------CORN</p>
<p>    May exports  560,792   Jan-May total exports   1,092,338</p>
<p> CUSTOMS		 May	 Pct	   Jan-May	Pct</p>
<p>    Tianjing	     0	 0.0		119	   0.01</p>
<p>    Dalian	 472,039	84.1	  908,580	  83.1</p>
<p>    Shenyang	23,946	 4.3	   35,965	   3.3</p>
<p>    Shenyang	45,180	 8.1	  118,104	  10.8</p>
<p>DESTINATIONS</p>
<p>    South Korea  213,025	38.0	 300,942	   27.6</p>
<p>    Malaysia     177,159	31.6	 359,967	   33.0</p>
<p>------RICE</p>
<p>    May exports  109,886   Jan-May total exports    272,421</p>
<p> CUSTOMS		 May	 Pct	   Jan-May	Pct</p>
<p>    Nanjing	 39,250	35.7	   91,954	  33.8</p>
<p>    Shanghai	26,553	24.2	   50,097	  18.4</p>
<p>    Ningbo	  15,392	14.0	   15,392	   5.7</p>
